            <ArticleTitle>Metastatic skeletal leiomyomatosis (leiomyomatosis ossea).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a unique case of metastatic leiomyomatosis to the skeleton. The very extensive involvement of the axial and peripheral skeleton with &quot;ring&quot; lesions and associated cyclical premenstrual pain eventually led to the correct diagnosis and total relief with hormonal therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
